{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and motion capabilities, separating sensor outcomes from motion commands. The specification binds sensor states to safe, progress-oriented actions: random_walk in clear, short forward pulses, and conservative turn recovery on obstacles. Recovery states are one-shot and only allow a single turn or scan action, returning to exploration as soon as the path is clear. Full_rotate is reserved for repeated or ambiguous blockages. All uncontrollables are handled in every state, and the supervisor avoids oscillation and infinite loops.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to reflect open-loop actuation and sensor-driven transitions.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, progress-oriented exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward for short progress, and single-action recovery states for obstacles, with rapid return to exploration after path_clear."
